                <pb facs="0842" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.67/248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-11T10:00:00+02:00">April 11, 1939—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 11—8:16 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Department’s 23, April 7, 6 p.m. Conversations with French colleagues, the
                    Turkish Minister for Foreign Affairs and his collaborators, indicate that
                    annexation of the Hatay by Turkey was some time ago agreed to in principle by
                    France, the exact date remaining to be settled. The French are endeavoring to
                    avoid the appearance of unseemly haste in acceding to Turkish demands and the
                    Turks appear willing to cooperate within reason in this respect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
